        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital stay of your 88-year-old female patient, admitted on 29/10/2010 due to an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Diagnostic workup included chest X-ray confirming hyperinflation, arterial blood gas analysis revealing hypoxaemic respiratory failure, and blood tests showing elevated inflammatory markers. Pulse oximetry was monitored continuously. Treatment consisted of supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids for supportive care. The patient responded well to treatment with clinical improvement and stabilisation of oxygen saturation. She was discharged on 30/10/2010 with adjusted inhalation therapy and oral steroids. Please arrange close follow-up and consider pulmonary rehabilitation referral. Do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>"
            },
